-- \[Short description of non-trivial change.\]
+**Improvements**
+- Added `Session.timeout`, a default timeout for every request sent through
+  the session (including `Session.send` and followed redirects). A call's own
+  `timeout` takes precedence; `timeout=None` on the call falls back to the
+  session default, and `timeout=(None, None)` waits forever. Defaults to
+  `None`, so existing behavior is unchanged.
 
 
 2.34.2 (2026-05-14)
diff --git a/docs/user/advanced.rst b/docs/user/advanced.rst
index f5209a5..e73bab6 100644
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1120,6 +1120,26 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+Rather than repeating ``timeout=`` on every call, you can set a default on a
+:class:`Session <requests.Session>`. Every request sent through that session
+uses it unless the call passes its own timeout::
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    s.timeout = (3.05, 27)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')                   # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=60)       # this call waits up to 60s
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)     # None means "not given": uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=(None, None))  # this call waits forever
+
+:attr:`Session.timeout <requests.Session.timeout>` accepts the same values as
+the ``timeout`` argument, and also applies to redirects that request follows and
+to :meth:`Session.send <requests.Session.send>`. As with the session's other
+settings, a ``timeout`` of ``None`` on the call means "use the session's
+default", so a helper that forwards ``timeout=None`` keeps the default rather
+than silently disabling it. To wait forever for one call on a session that has
+a default, pass ``(None, None)``. The session default is ``None``: no timeout.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
